00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:46.640
I don't either.
我也不觉得。

616
00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:48.920
No, this is her thing.
不，这是她自己的事。

617
00:26:49.100 --> 00:26:49.880
This is her time.
这是属于她的时间。

618
00:26:50.140 --> 00:26:51.280
Because it's Colin Firth.
因为那是科林·费尔斯主演的。

619
00:26:53.140 --> 00:26:57.920
I used to do this at a job that I had as a media buyer.
我以前做媒体买手的时候也干过这种事。

620
00:26:58.200 --> 00:27:00.060
You would sneak off and watch movies?
你会溜出去看电影？

621
00:27:00.780 --> 00:27:07.000
Well, part of our job, because we bought time to advertise movies, part of our job was
嗯，因为我们的工作内容之一是购买电影广告时段，所以我们的工作的一部分就是

622
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:10.560
that we got to leave to go see screenings of movies.
我们可以离开办公室去参加电影试映会。

623
00:27:10.560 --> 00:27:11.600
It was really cool.
那真的很酷。

624
00:27:12.100 --> 00:27:17.440
But we would, after the movie, my girlfriend and I, who both worked there, around the corner
但看完电影后，我和在那儿工作的女朋友会去转角处

625
00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:20.660
from the screening area was a place where you get a manicure pedicure.
离试映区不远的地方有一家做美甲和足疗的店。

626
00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:24.920
And we would just tack one on to the end of our day out.
我们就会在一天结束时顺便去一下。

627
00:27:25.140 --> 00:27:26.200
It was kind of fun.
那还挺有趣的。

628
00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:30.900
That's the best, is when you have a job where there's an excuse for you to be out of the
那是最棒的，当你有一份工作，让你有借口可以待在

629
00:27:30.900 --> 00:27:31.320
office.
办公室外面。

630
00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:32.180
Right.
没错。

631
00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:35.640
That's slightly fuzzy about when you're going to get back.
那种对什么时候回去有点模糊的感觉。

632
00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:36.160
Yeah.
是啊。

633
00:27:36.380 --> 00:27:36.580
Yeah.
没错。

634
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:37.560
Exactly.
确实。

635
00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:40.120
I did do this when I interned on Conan.
我在柯南秀实习的时候也干过这事。

636
00:27:40.120 --> 00:27:44.780
If they would send us on a run, you would just go sit for a little bit in a coffee shop.
如果他们派我们去跑腿，你就会找个咖啡馆坐一会儿。

637
00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:45.700
Take your time.
慢慢来。

638
00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:46.540
Have a snack.
吃点零食。

639
00:27:47.460 --> 00:27:49.200
Enjoy a tea in Central Park.
在中央公园喝杯茶享受一下。

640
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:55.960
I was a proofreader in one job, and it was in a very small publishing house.
我有一份工作是校对员，那是一家非常小的出版社。

641
00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:58.760
It was in a guy's house, and he had a three-story house.
它就在一个人的家里，那是一栋三层楼的房子。

642
00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:01.060
And there were two, I had two bosses.
我有两个老板。

643
00:28:01.420 --> 00:28:03.920
One of them was on the first floor, and one of them was on the third floor.
一个在一楼，另一个在三楼。

644
00:28:04.120 --> 00:28:04.340
Okay.
好吧。

645
00:28:04.660 --> 00:28:06.900
And sometimes I would just go to the second floor.
有时候我就躲到二楼去。

646
00:28:08.500 --> 00:28:10.560
And they always think you were with the other.
他们总以为我在另一个老板那里。

647
00:28:10.580 --> 00:28:10.760
Yeah.
是啊。

648
00:28:10.940 --> 00:28:14.920
They were like, oh, he must be down on the first floor working on that guy project.
他们会说，噢，他肯定在一楼忙那个项目呢。

649
00:28:16.180 --> 00:28:19.520
Well, Michael is going to have his very last conference room meeting, Greg.
格雷格，迈克尔要进行他最后一次会议室会议了。

650
00:28:20.040 --> 00:28:23.900
Did you think a lot about how you wanted him to have a conference room meeting in this episode?
你有没有仔细考虑过你想让他在这集里以怎样的方式进行会议室会议？

651
00:28:24.440 --> 00:28:27.900
Well, I think he's getting panicked because his time is running out.
我觉得他开始慌了，因为他的时间不多了。

652
00:28:28.060 --> 00:28:28.360
Right.
没错。

653
00:28:28.360 --> 00:28:31.300
And I think that he enjoyed conference room meetings.
而且我觉得他很享受会议室里的会议。

654
00:28:31.500 --> 00:28:31.820
Yeah.
是啊。

655
00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:35.440
Because he was able to use them as tryouts for his stand-up.
因为他能把这些会议当成他单口喜剧的试演场。

656
00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:37.300
Exactly.
确实。

657
00:28:37.740 --> 00:28:38.480
And have a captive audience.
而且还有一群不得不听的观众。

658
00:28:38.820 --> 00:28:39.460
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

659
00:28:39.520 --> 00:28:42.300
So he calls them without really knowing what he's going to say, I think.
所以我觉得他召集会议时，其实根本不知道自己要说什么。

660
00:28:42.480 --> 00:28:46.660
Which is very on brand, because I feel like Michael called a lot of meetings like that.
这很符合他的风格，因为我觉得迈克尔经常那样召集会议。

661
00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:46.980
Yeah.
是啊。

662
00:28:46.980 --> 00:28:52.460
I was very sad that I was not in the last conference room meeting.
我很难过自己没能参加最后那场会议室会议。

663
00:28:52.840 --> 00:28:54.240
This was a bummer for me.
这让我挺沮丧的。

664
00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:56.500
These are some of my happiest times on set.
那是我在片场最快乐的时光之一。

665
00:28:56.840 --> 00:28:57.020
Yeah.
是啊。

666
00:28:57.520 --> 00:28:58.220
That was rough.
那确实很难受。

667
00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:03.420
Well, if you go to 28 minutes and three seconds, I know this is what everyone's looking for in this scene.
如果你看到28分03秒，我知道这正是大家在这场戏里想找的细节。

668
00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:05.120
My hair is back in the clip again.
我的头发又夹回发夹里了。

669
00:29:05.320 --> 00:29:06.020
Oh, good.
哦，太好了。

670
00:29:06.260 --> 00:29:07.720
The continuity has returned.
连贯性终于回来了。

671
00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:09.640
That's what struck me the first time when we saw this.
我们第一次看到这儿的时候，我就被这一点吸引了。

672
00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:10.280
I was like.
我当时就在想。

673
00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:11.620
What's up with Angela's hair clip?
安吉拉的发夹是怎么回事？

674
00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:12.500
Angela's hair's back.
安吉拉的头发又变回去了。

675
00:29:12.760 --> 00:29:13.040
Yeah.
是啊。

676
00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:15.360
All will be right with the world.
一切又回归正常了。

677
00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:22.380
Well, in this conference room meeting, Jim is going to figure out that something is going on.
在这场会议室会议中，吉姆开始察觉到有些不对劲。

678
00:29:22.460 --> 00:29:25.380
And he asks Michael if he can speak to him in his office.
他问迈克尔能不能去办公室和他谈谈。

679
00:29:25.700 --> 00:29:27.880
I mean, Michael's getting a little unhinged.
我是说，迈克尔开始有点失控了。

680
00:29:28.100 --> 00:29:28.420
Yes.
没错。

681
00:29:28.640 --> 00:29:30.360
And Jim is the most perceptive.
而吉姆是最敏锐的。

682
00:29:31.460 --> 00:29:31.720
Yes.
是的。

683
00:29:31.900 --> 00:29:34.260
So he is the one who's going to figure this out.
所以他会是那个发现真相的人。

684
00:29:34.480 --> 00:29:37.940
When did you decide that Jim was going to be the person who figures it out?
你们是什么时候决定让吉姆成为那个发现真相的人的？

685
00:29:38.240 --> 00:29:41.120
Well, you know, everybody has their moment with Michael.
嗯，你知道，每个人都会和迈克尔有属于他们的时刻。

686
00:29:41.120 --> 00:29:51.880
Well, and Jim, it just seems like Michael is sort of graduating psychologically into being a wiser character here.
而且对于吉姆来说，迈克尔在这里似乎在心理上逐渐成长为一个更睿智的角色。

687
00:29:51.880 --> 00:29:55.960
And, you know, as he's going to float above the office into the clouds.
而且，你知道，他就像要从办公室升入云端一样。

688
00:29:56.100 --> 00:29:56.380
Yes.
是的。

689
00:29:57.660 --> 00:30:01.420
And there is like this little ruse going in the middle of the show.
剧集中间还有个小小的计谋。

690
00:30:01.880 --> 00:30:08.360
And for Jim to have a moment and not be in on it, it seemed like it was good for his character that he figures it out.
让吉姆有一个时刻，而且他没参与其中，我觉得让他发现真相这对他的角色塑造很有好处。

691
00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:12.100
And they can have the only like sincere conversation.
这样他们就能进行唯一一次真诚的对话。

692
00:30:12.780 --> 00:30:15.180
But again, we started to roll on the last day.
但再说一次，我们是在最后一天开拍的。

693
00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:17.460
And it was the only sincere conversation.
那是唯一一次真诚的对话。

694
00:30:18.160 --> 00:30:20.040
And it got very emotional.
而且当时非常感人。

695
00:30:20.480 --> 00:30:20.580
Yeah.
是啊。

696
00:30:20.700 --> 00:30:26.980
This was the second to last scene that we shot that day was the scene between Michael and Jim and Michael's office.
那天我们拍摄的倒数第二场戏，就是迈克尔和吉姆在迈克尔办公室里的那场戏。

697
00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:34.220
Well, if you guys have the DVD box set, it's definitely worth watching this scene because it's a bigger scene.
如果你们有DVD套装，绝对值得看看这场戏，因为原版更长。

698
00:30:34.520 --> 00:30:42.200
There is this great beat in the middle of it, Greg, which I understand why it was probably deleted just because the flow of the scene is so perfect.
格雷格，中间有个很棒的停顿，我明白为什么它可能被删掉了，因为这场戏的节奏已经非常完美了。

699
00:30:42.200 --> 00:30:44.340
But it's such a great detail.
但那是一个非常棒的细节。

700
00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:49.560
So Michael is going to share with Jim that he has a job interview already set up in Colorado.
所以迈克尔要告诉吉姆，他已经在科罗拉多安排好了一场面试。

701
00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:55.220
It's for a paper company that makes the ticket stubs for all the movie theaters.
那是给一家造纸公司做的，他们专门生产所有电影院用的票根。

702
00:30:55.760 --> 00:30:57.640
And he says, you know, it's perfect.
他说，你知道，这太完美了。

703
00:30:57.800 --> 00:31:00.140
It combines both my loves, movies and paper.
它结合了我两个爱好，电影和纸张。

704
00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:02.620
And I just thought that was such a great detail.
我当时觉得这个细节真是太棒了。

705
00:31:02.860 --> 00:31:08.480
I like to know in my brain, like, you know, where Michael is, where he's living, what he's up to.
我喜欢在脑海里清楚地知道，迈克尔在哪里，他住在哪里，他在忙些什么。

706
00:31:08.480 --> 00:31:12.620
And I just sort of see him working for the ticket stub paper company.
我总觉得他应该是在那家票根造纸公司工作。

707
00:31:12.980 --> 00:31:13.140
Yeah.
没错。

708
00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:18.260
Well, you know, my dad had two great friends growing up, Dick Town and Tom Hazen.
嗯，我父亲小时候有两个好朋友，迪克·汤恩和汤姆·黑森。

709
00:31:18.400 --> 00:31:19.480
And I can't remember which one.
我不记得是哪一个了。

710
00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:21.760
One of them had a family paper company.
他们其中一人家里经营着一家造纸公司。

711
00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:25.160
And they transitioned into tickets.
后来他们转型做了票据。

712
00:31:25.480 --> 00:31:29.600
And that saved a lot of small, or at least it really helped.
这拯救了许多小型造纸厂，或者说至少帮了大忙。

713
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:30.920
Small paper companies?
小型造纸厂？

714
00:31:30.920 --> 00:31:33.840
That small paper company because it was a very high-tech form of paper.
就是那家小型造纸厂，因为那是一种技术含量很高的纸。

715
00:31:33.840 --> 00:31:37.120
It had all these embossed, you know, things in it and everything.
上面有各种压花之类的东西，应有尽有。

716
00:31:37.320 --> 00:31:41.760
I was probably on somebody's phone now, so it's probably, it was only a temporary reprieve.
我现在可能又在谁的电话里了，所以这可能只是暂时的解脱。

717
00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:44.300
But I remember being told that around that time.
但我记得当时有人跟我说过这件事。

718
00:31:44.700 --> 00:31:52.600
And it did seem like a great job for Michael because it was paper, but it was a little show-busy form of paper, you know.
这对于迈克尔来说确实是一份很棒的工作，因为它是纸张生意，但又带点演艺圈的色彩，你懂的。

719
00:31:53.580 --> 00:32:05.520
But the thing about that scene is when it got so sort of real and John was saying stuff to the actor, Steve Carell, about how he felt about working with him for seven years,
但那场戏的关键在于，当它变得非常真实，约翰对演员史蒂夫·卡瑞尔说起他这七年来与他共事的感受时，

720
00:32:05.720 --> 00:32:07.940
it started to really spread.
那种情绪真的开始蔓延开来。

721
00:32:08.140 --> 00:32:11.520
And you were like, God, this can't be an eight-minute scene.
你会觉得，天哪，这不该是一场八分钟的戏。

722
00:32:11.520 --> 00:32:15.480
And, you know, so we were throwing lines out, you know, in the editing room.
所以，你知道，我们在剪辑室里删减了很多台词。

723
00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:20.300
It was just, it was just down to the sort of the nub version of it.
最后只留下了最核心的部分。

724
00:32:20.400 --> 00:32:22.660
But it was, it came out well, I think.
但我认为效果很好。

725
00:32:22.760 --> 00:32:24.740
And it was emotional to watch them.
看着他们真的很感人。

726
00:32:25.060 --> 00:32:33.420
It was emotional to rewatch when, you know, Jim says, but we clearly just saw John in the moment saying when he said, you're the best boss I've ever had.
重看的时候也很感人，当吉姆说出那句“你是我遇到过最好的老板”时，我们很清楚地看到那一刻约翰是真情流露。

727
00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.520
I was just like, forget it.
我当时就想，算了吧。

728
00:32:35.680 --> 00:32:35.860
Yeah.
是啊。

729
00:32:36.040 --> 00:32:37.200
I'm a mess.
我彻底崩溃了。

730
00:32:37.520 --> 00:32:39.860
George Clooney and Leatherheads didn't compare.
乔治·克鲁尼和《爱情达阵》根本没法比。

731
00:32:42.480 --> 00:32:45.220
We had a fan catch from Juliana R.
我们收到了一位粉丝的发现，来自佐治亚州亚特兰大的朱莉安娜·R。

732
00:32:45.340 --> 00:32:49.340
in Atlanta, Georgia, who said, I have a fan catch.
她说，我有一个粉丝发现。

733
00:32:49.480 --> 00:32:52.840
Michael forgot his voice recorder in his desk on the last day.
迈克尔在最后一天把录音机忘在办公桌里了。

734
00:32:53.460 --> 00:32:59.320
You know, in that scene, he gets out his voice recorder because he has a T-shirt idea, goodbye, stink.
你知道，在那场戏里，他拿出了录音机，因为他想到了一个T恤的点子，“再见，臭家伙”。

735
00:32:59.320 --> 00:32:59.680
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
哦，对，对，对。

736
00:32:59.780 --> 00:33:01.280
And then he puts it back in the drawer.
然后他把它放回了抽屉里。

737
00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:02.340
And he left without it.
结果他走的时候没带走它。

738
00:33:02.420 --> 00:33:02.760
Yes.
是的。

739
00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:03.480
Justin A.
来自纽约州布法罗的贾斯汀·A。

740
00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:07.380
from Buffalo, New York noticed this as well and wanted to know, was this an intentional joke?
也注意到了这一点，想知道这是否是一个刻意的笑话？

741
00:33:07.480 --> 00:33:08.780
Because they both really enjoyed it.
因为他们俩都很喜欢这个细节。

742
00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:10.760
They both enjoyed the fact that he forgot to bring it.
他们都很喜欢他忘了带走录音机这个事实。

743
00:33:10.760 --> 00:33:11.260
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

744
00:33:11.260 --> 00:33:15.700
That he left his, he walks out without his voice recorder with all his good ideas on it.
他走的时候没带走那个存着他所有好点子的录音机。

745
00:33:16.160 --> 00:33:16.400
Yeah.
没错。

746
00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:17.040
Oh, goodness.
天哪。

747
00:33:17.320 --> 00:33:21.920
I don't think that was intentional, but I'm glad that they're perceiving it as a joke.
我不觉得那是刻意的，但我很高兴他们把它当成了一个笑话。

748
00:33:22.080 --> 00:33:22.460
Own it.
那就认领了吧。

749
00:33:22.720 --> 00:33:22.940
Yeah.
是啊。

750
00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:23.520
Yes.
没错。

751
00:33:23.520 --> 00:33:27.780
I like the idea that it's a wonderful leave behind for the next boss.
我很喜欢这个点子，这对他下一任老板来说是一份很棒的遗产。

752
00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:28.120
Right.
没错。

753
00:33:28.580 --> 00:33:30.920
A drawer full of amazing ideas.
抽屉里装满了奇思妙想。

754
00:33:32.100 --> 00:33:33.720
I like that T-shirt, yeah.
我很喜欢那件T恤，真的。

755
00:33:34.620 --> 00:33:35.360
I love that.
我太喜欢那个了。

756
00:33:35.440 --> 00:33:40.800
I mean, that was a running thing for Michael as a character is that he would sometimes interrupt
我是说，迈克尔这个角色的一个惯用梗就是他有时会打断

757
00:33:40.800 --> 00:33:44.580
himself to have a great idea that were always terrible.
自己，然后冒出一个绝妙的点子，但其实总是很糟糕。

758
00:33:44.860 --> 00:33:46.100
Do you do that as a writer?
你作为编剧也会这样吗？

759
00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:50.880
Are you ever somewhere or at dinner, do you have a place where you put observations or ideas?
你平时在外面或者吃晚饭时，有没有专门记录观察或点子的地方？

760
00:33:51.620 --> 00:33:53.140
Do you have a writer's notebook?
你有编剧笔记本吗？

761
00:33:53.140 --> 00:33:58.120
I have scraps because I don't ever have the special writer's notebook with me.
我只有零碎的纸片，因为我从没随身带过那种专业的编剧笔记本。

762
00:33:58.220 --> 00:33:58.580
Of course.
当然。

763
00:33:58.580 --> 00:34:05.240
So, but I do have a box in my house and I'll tear, you know, I'll throw in the napkin or
所以，我家里有个盒子，我会把餐巾纸或者

764
00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:06.960
the back of the envelope.
信封背面撕下来，扔进去。

765
00:34:07.300 --> 00:34:07.640
Yeah.
是啊。

766
00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:09.020
And I'll throw it into the box.
然后我就把它们扔进盒子里。

767
00:34:09.240 --> 00:34:12.540
And then, so then you sit down, you have to write a new script or come up with a new
那么当你坐下来，需要写新剧本或者构思一个新

768
00:34:12.540 --> 00:34:12.900
character.
角色时。

769
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:17.920
Do you open the box and it's like, you look for the magical scrap that's going to be the
你会打开盒子，寻找那个能成为灵感种子的

770
00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:18.240
seed?
神奇纸片吗？

771
00:34:18.240 --> 00:34:19.380
Pod over scraps.
翻遍那些碎纸片。

772
00:34:20.040 --> 00:34:23.280
They're down to like really useless scraps at this point.
到了现在，里面剩下的都是些毫无用处的废纸了。

773
00:34:23.540 --> 00:34:25.180
I've used everything I possibly can.
我能用的都已经用光了。

774
00:34:26.200 --> 00:34:27.720
Well, why don't we take a break?
好吧，我们要不要休息一下？

775
00:34:27.720 --> 00:34:33.920
Because when we come back, it's Michael's last bullpen scene ever.
因为回来之后，就是迈克尔在办公区的最后一场戏了。

776
00:34:34.640 --> 00:34:35.540
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

777
00:34:44.650 --> 00:34:46.750
Well, we are back and here it is.
好了，我们回来了，就是这一幕。

778
00:34:47.030 --> 00:34:49.650
This is Michael's last bullpen scene.
这是迈克尔在办公区的最后一场戏。

779
00:34:49.890 --> 00:34:53.570
This is the last thing we filmed with Steve Carell on The Office.
这是我们在《办公室》里和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔拍摄的最后一个镜头。

780
00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:56.130
He just walks out into the bullpen.
他只是走进了办公区。

781
00:34:56.130 --> 00:35:02.210
He takes his unfinished mittens from Phyllis and he just stands there and looks at this
他拿过菲利斯织了一半的手套，就那样站着，看着这

782
00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:03.230
ordinary workday.
平凡的工作日。

783
00:35:03.750 --> 00:35:12.450
I remember going to the mix for this and cranking the sounds, the ordinary sounds of The Office.
我记得当时去混音，把声音调大，那些《办公室》里平凡的声音。

784
00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:15.950
The phones ringing and the fax machines and stuff.
电话铃声、传真机声之类的。

785
00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:17.230
Yeah, and we had tons of those.
对，我们有成堆那样的音效。

786
00:35:17.410 --> 00:35:22.950
We had tracks for every type of like dot matrix printer, you know, over the years.
多年来，我们有各种针式打印机的音轨。

787
00:35:22.950 --> 00:35:26.870
And we just sort of like threw it all in, like, you know, jack it up.
我们只是把它们都加进去，你知道，把音量调大。

788
00:35:26.990 --> 00:35:33.010
And there was this, I thought it was something where it was like an opportunity to just remind
我觉得这是一个机会，可以提醒

789
00:35:33.010 --> 00:35:35.390
people of the sound of what it was.
观众那是什么样的声音。

790
00:35:35.530 --> 00:35:39.250
So to me, the sound was as important as the picture on that thing.
所以对我来说，那段戏里声音和画面一样重要。

791
00:35:39.870 --> 00:35:45.130
You know, in the finale, you gave Pam that line about the beauty of ordinary things.
你知道，在大结局里，你让帕姆说了那句关于平凡事物之美的话。

792
00:35:45.130 --> 00:35:45.610
Yeah.
是啊。

793
00:35:45.810 --> 00:35:48.710
But I feel like that is the story of this episode as well.
但我觉得那也是这一集的主题。

794
00:35:48.930 --> 00:35:49.910
Yeah, it's in here for sure.
没错，这集里肯定有。

795
00:35:50.150 --> 00:35:50.830
Yeah, that theme.
对，那个主题。

796
00:35:51.090 --> 00:35:51.770
It's here.
它就在这里。

797
00:35:51.990 --> 00:35:52.310
Yeah.
是啊。

798
00:35:52.530 --> 00:35:57.670
Well, it's inherent in a documentary that you're looking at real people.
毕竟纪录片的本质就是观察真实的人。

799
00:35:58.190 --> 00:35:58.530
Yeah.
没错。

800
00:35:58.950 --> 00:36:02.310
But that goes back to that poor guy who retired from SoCal gas.
但这又回到了那个从南加州天然气公司退休的可怜人身上。

801
00:36:02.570 --> 00:36:03.930
Yeah, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

802
00:36:04.350 --> 00:36:04.750
Yeah.
是啊。

803
00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:05.070
Yeah.
对。

804
00:36:05.450 --> 00:36:06.350
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

805
00:36:06.590 --> 00:36:11.470
Because I, so I was not in the scene, but I was there because after we shot this day,
因为我当时不在拍摄现场，但我确实在那儿，因为那天拍完后，

806
00:36:11.510 --> 00:36:13.850
we had a big goodbye party for Steve.
我们为史蒂夫举办了一场盛大的欢送派对。

807
00:36:14.030 --> 00:36:17.410
So I had come up to the set and I wanted to see his last scene in the bullpen.
所以我去了片场，想看他最后在办公区的戏份。

808
00:36:17.610 --> 00:36:20.190
So I was at Video Village and I was watching this.
当时我在监视器旁看着这一幕。

809
00:36:20.570 --> 00:36:26.190
And I remember that we did do a version where Michael turns out all the lights on everybody
我记得我们确实拍过一个版本，迈克尔在离开时，

810
00:36:26.190 --> 00:36:27.010
as he's leaving.
把所有人的灯都关了。

811
00:36:27.430 --> 00:36:27.510
Yeah.
没错。

812
00:36:27.570 --> 00:36:28.270
Do you remember that?
你记得吗？

813
00:36:28.430 --> 00:36:28.510
Yeah.
记得。

814
00:36:28.670 --> 00:36:30.290
We like yell at him like Michael.
我们就像冲他喊“迈克尔”那样。

815
00:36:30.290 --> 00:36:32.690
Yes, that was going to be the big joke.
对，那本来是个大笑点。

816
00:36:32.850 --> 00:36:33.090
Right.
没错。

817
00:36:33.310 --> 00:36:37.390
That he assumed that when he left, the whole thing was that nobody needed to have light.
他以为他一走，大家就不需要光了。

818
00:36:37.810 --> 00:36:38.250
Exactly.
正是如此。

819
00:36:38.670 --> 00:36:38.870
Yeah.
是啊。

820
00:36:39.410 --> 00:36:46.410
I think that was hard too, because their windows, I don't think it was as like, I know we shot
我觉得那段也很难处理，因为窗户的关系，我不觉得……我知道我们拍了，

821
00:36:46.410 --> 00:36:46.610
it.
拍了。

822
00:36:46.670 --> 00:36:46.870
Yeah.
对。

823
00:36:47.230 --> 00:36:52.430
And I remember it, I think we had some problems with it from an emotional standpoint is like
我记得从情感角度来看，我们遇到了一些问题，因为

824
00:36:52.430 --> 00:36:57.630
it was kind of negative when it was otherwise a very positive sort of beat.
这在原本非常积极的基调中显得有些消极。

825
00:36:57.630 --> 00:37:01.890
But I also think it didn't execute enormously well because of the windows.
而且我觉得因为窗户的原因，效果也不是特别好。

826
00:37:02.170 --> 00:37:04.570
So it's like it didn't get really that dark.
所以看起来并没有真正暗下来。

827
00:37:05.730 --> 00:37:06.850
So, you know.
所以，你知道的。

828
00:37:07.150 --> 00:37:07.410
Yeah.
是啊。

829
00:37:07.630 --> 00:37:07.830
Yeah.
对。

830
00:37:08.010 --> 00:37:13.510
So there's a great moment at the end when Michael's watching everyone work and Jim clocks
最后有个很棒的时刻，迈克尔看着大家工作，吉姆注意到了

831
00:37:13.510 --> 00:37:14.010
Michael.
迈克尔。

832
00:37:14.510 --> 00:37:19.210
And Greg, you shared on the commentary that it wasn't scripted, but that the camera guys
格雷格，你在评论音轨里分享过，那不是剧本写的，而是摄影师

833
00:37:19.210 --> 00:37:23.170
just caught the moment and that you loved it and it was so perfect.
刚好捕捉到了那一刻，你很喜欢，觉得非常完美。

834
00:37:23.450 --> 00:37:26.070
Is that where Jim kind of gives him a little like you can go?
就是吉姆示意他可以走了的那种感觉吗？

835
00:37:26.210 --> 00:37:26.430
Yeah.
对。

836
00:37:26.430 --> 00:37:27.210
You got this.
你懂的。

837
00:37:27.210 --> 00:37:27.470
Yeah.
没错。

838
00:37:27.470 --> 00:37:27.690
Yeah.
是啊。

839
00:37:27.810 --> 00:37:29.710
Like a little head, like get out of here.
就像点头示意他快走吧。

840
00:37:29.890 --> 00:37:30.090
Yeah.
对。

841
00:37:30.410 --> 00:37:31.190
Kind of head nod.
算是点头示意。

842
00:37:31.630 --> 00:37:34.370
And Michael smiles and nods and then he walks out.
然后迈克尔笑了笑，点点头，走了出去。

843
00:37:34.550 --> 00:37:34.730
Yeah.
没错。

844
00:37:34.870 --> 00:37:39.270
And we know he's going to heaven paradise with Holly.
我们知道他要去和霍莉过天堂般的生活了。

845
00:37:39.630 --> 00:37:44.570
But there's also a little bit of like Michael's at the deathbed of his dad.
但也有点像迈克尔在他父亲临终床前的感觉。

846
00:37:44.730 --> 00:37:48.450
I guess that's where Brent's getting this from because he's like, I release you.
我想布伦特就是从这儿联想到的，因为他就像是在说“我放你走了”。

847
00:37:48.710 --> 00:37:48.930
Yeah.
是啊。

848
00:37:48.930 --> 00:37:49.550
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

849
00:37:49.690 --> 00:37:49.890
Yeah.
明白。

850
00:37:50.110 --> 00:37:50.330
Yeah.
对。

851
00:37:50.510 --> 00:37:55.370
And he maybe needed that last little look from Jim, that last little nudge of like assurance.
也许他当时确实需要吉姆最后看他的那一眼，需要那最后一点点鼓励。

852
00:37:55.370 --> 00:37:55.830
That'll be okay.
没问题的。

853
00:37:55.990 --> 00:37:56.170
Yeah.
是啊。

854
00:37:56.330 --> 00:37:56.470
Yeah.
没错。

855
00:37:56.970 --> 00:38:02.850
Well, I remember Nancy Carell had come up and was watching this last scene as well.
我记得南希·卡瑞尔当时也走过来，和我们一起看了这场最后的戏。

856
00:38:03.010 --> 00:38:03.270
Yeah.
是啊。

857
00:38:03.490 --> 00:38:04.230
On the monitors.
在监视器上看的。

858
00:38:04.510 --> 00:38:06.010
And that was really special.
那真的很特别。

859
00:38:06.010 --> 00:38:10.910
And from a personal standpoint, I remember standing in the conference room.
从个人角度来说，我记得当时站在会议室里。

860
00:38:11.070 --> 00:38:11.990
Michael's realtor?
迈克尔的房产经纪人？

861
00:38:12.270 --> 00:38:12.690
Why would she?
她为什么要来？

862
00:38:13.810 --> 00:38:14.410
Carol?
卡罗尔？

863
00:38:14.570 --> 00:38:16.710
Carol wanted to be there.
卡罗尔想在那儿。

864
00:38:16.710 --> 00:38:22.790
But I remember being in the conference room and I was pregnant when we shot this episode.
但我记得当时在会议室里，拍这一集的时候我怀孕了。

865
00:38:22.970 --> 00:38:25.190
And I had not told anyone except for Angela.
除了安吉拉，我没告诉任何人。

866
00:38:25.730 --> 00:38:33.970
And I remember just wrestling with whether or not I should tell Nancy or if I should get Steve aside because I did not know when I would see them again.
我记得当时一直在纠结要不要告诉南希，或者把史蒂夫叫到一边说，因为我不知道下次见到他们是什么时候了。

867
00:38:34.130 --> 00:38:39.150
And all Steve ever wanted was for me to have the family that I always wanted.
史蒂夫一直以来最希望的就是我能拥有我梦寐以求的家庭。

868
00:38:39.150 --> 00:38:42.410
So, I just knew how excited he would be for me.
所以我知道他会为我感到多么高兴。

869
00:38:42.650 --> 00:38:44.070
I did not tell them.
我没告诉他们。

870
00:38:44.290 --> 00:38:45.270
I stayed quiet.
我保持了沉默。

871
00:38:45.270 --> 00:38:47.370
I remember urging you to have a baby.
我记得我当时一直催你生个孩子。

872
00:38:47.550 --> 00:38:51.290
Greg, you were urging me to have a baby from like the pilot.
格雷格，你从试播集开始就一直在催我生孩子了。

873
00:38:51.570 --> 00:38:55.250
Like all you did was go around and encourage cast members to start families.
你整天到处鼓励演员们组建家庭。

874
00:38:55.730 --> 00:38:59.290
Because you are such a family guy and you love family.
因为你是个顾家的人，你热爱家庭。

875
00:38:59.450 --> 00:39:00.850
And I do remember this though.
不过我确实记得这件事。

876
00:39:00.990 --> 00:39:03.410
You were like, when are you guys going to start having babies?
你当时问，你们什么时候打算要孩子？

877
00:39:03.410 --> 00:39:07.210
Well, I also felt really because it was countered the interests as a producer.
嗯，我也觉得很有必要，因为这和制片人的利益是相悖的。

878
00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:12.690
And I always felt like I just want to make sure I'm completely on record as supporting anybody having a baby.
我一直觉得我得明确表态，我是支持任何人要孩子的。

879
00:39:12.810 --> 00:39:16.090
The last thing I want for somebody to come back and go, I missed having a baby.
我最不希望看到的就是有人回头说，我因为工作错过了生孩子。

880
00:39:16.310 --> 00:39:16.650
Right, right.
对，没错。

881
00:39:16.690 --> 00:39:19.410
I felt pressure not to have a baby or something.
觉得有压力不能生孩子之类的。

882
00:39:19.670 --> 00:39:20.050
But yeah.
不过确实。

883
00:39:20.650 --> 00:39:20.970
Yeah.
是啊。

884
00:39:21.150 --> 00:39:28.810
But I just remember holding on to that little secret while I was standing there watching this last scene and wondering when am I ever going to see Steve again?
但我记得当时站在那儿看最后一场戏时，我一直守着这个小秘密，心里想着我到底什么时候才能再见到史蒂夫？

885
00:39:29.410 --> 00:39:31.170
Well, you probably did the right thing.
嗯，你可能做对了。

886
00:39:31.390 --> 00:39:32.830
This is a big moment in their lives.
这对他们来说是人生中的重要时刻。

887
00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:34.250
So it's probably, you know.
所以，你知道的。

888
00:39:34.590 --> 00:39:35.910
Maybe I shouldn't have made it about me.
也许我不该把焦点转到自己身上。

889
00:39:38.330 --> 00:39:39.230
Goodbye, Steve.
再见，史蒂夫。

890
00:39:39.490 --> 00:39:40.210
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

891
00:39:40.390 --> 00:39:41.450
I'm having a burger.
我在吃汉堡。

892
00:39:41.450 --> 00:39:42.030
Hey, everybody.
嘿，各位。

893
00:39:42.290 --> 00:39:46.810
I'm pregnant after we wrap.
杀青后我怀孕了。

894
00:39:47.010 --> 00:39:48.370
Yeah, it's down in the warehouse.
就在仓库下面。

895
00:39:49.430 --> 00:39:52.390
In the corner, there's a going away party for Steve.
角落里正在为史蒂夫举办欢送会。

896
00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:53.750
But the real party.
但真正的派对是。

897
00:39:57.530 --> 00:40:01.370
Michael is going to have a talking head that he got to say goodbye to almost everyone.
迈克尔会有一个采访镜头，说他得以和几乎每个人都道了别。

898
00:40:01.490 --> 00:40:03.590
And that Holly is his family now.
而且霍莉现在就是他的家人了。

899
00:40:04.150 --> 00:40:09.070
But right before this talking head, there would have been a deleted scene between Michael and Hank.
但在这一采访镜头之前，原本还有一段迈克尔和汉克的删减戏份。

900
00:40:09.730 --> 00:40:11.710
And Michael's waiting for his taxi.
当时迈克尔正在等他的出租车。

901
00:40:11.970 --> 00:40:16.510
But he decides to buy one last cup of coffee from Hank and tries to give Hank a big tip.
但他决定从汉克那里买最后一杯咖啡，并试图给汉克一大笔小费。

902
00:40:16.670 --> 00:40:18.930
And then Hank, you know, gives him a lot of sass.
然后汉克，你知道的，对他说了不少刻薄话。

903
00:40:19.090 --> 00:40:20.630
And then it just all backfires.
结果反而弄巧成拙了。

904
00:40:20.870 --> 00:40:23.370
It was just like perfect Hank-Michael scenario.
这简直是典型的汉克与迈克尔式场景。

905
00:40:23.370 --> 00:40:25.670
Hugh was a great actor.
休是一位伟大的演员。

906
00:40:25.910 --> 00:40:27.010
And they had a relationship.
他们之间有过一段交情。

907
00:40:27.290 --> 00:40:28.970
And that should have been in the show.
那段戏本该出现在剧集里的。

908
00:40:29.130 --> 00:40:30.930
But it was awkwardly placed.
但它放的位置有点尴尬。

909
00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:33.530
Because we were racing towards the ending now.
因为我们当时正赶着大结局。

910
00:40:33.730 --> 00:40:34.130
Yes.
是的。

911
00:40:34.330 --> 00:40:37.390
We didn't really have time to slow it down again and have this interaction.
我们确实没有时间再放慢节奏去加入这段互动了。

912
00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:38.090
Yes.
是的。

913
00:40:38.090 --> 00:40:39.150
But it is a deleted scene.
但它作为删减片段保留了下来。

914
00:40:39.230 --> 00:40:39.990
It's nice to see.
能看到它真好。

915
00:40:40.170 --> 00:40:44.270
Because it works so well that the taxi pulls up when Michael's with Jim.
因为迈克尔和吉姆在一起时出租车开过来，这一幕效果非常好。

916
00:40:44.490 --> 00:40:44.710
Yeah.
没错。

917
00:40:44.930 --> 00:40:45.250
You know?
你懂的吧？

918
00:40:45.250 --> 00:40:46.190
And it's so abrupt.
而且非常突然。

919
00:40:46.190 --> 00:40:46.790
He's leaving.
他要走了。

920
00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:50.970
And so to then have this extra beat where then he's waiting for his taxi.
所以如果再加一段他等出租车的戏，就显得多余了。

921
00:40:51.270 --> 00:40:51.510
Yeah.
没错。

922
00:40:51.630 --> 00:40:57.370
I think it was also sort of conceived of as his really is lingering because he wants to see Pam.
我想这段戏最初的构思是，他之所以徘徊不前，是因为他想见帕姆。

923
00:40:57.550 --> 00:40:59.770
But that was sort of implied elsewhere.
但这在其他地方已经有所暗示了。

924
00:41:00.150 --> 00:41:00.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

925
00:41:00.810 --> 00:41:02.730
Well, he is going to get to see Pam.
好吧，他确实会见到帕姆。

926
00:41:02.910 --> 00:41:03.930
We don't know it yet.
我们现在还不知道这一点。

927
00:41:04.050 --> 00:41:04.250
Yes.
是的。

928
00:41:04.350 --> 00:41:06.010
But we follow Michael to the airport.
但我们跟随迈克尔去了机场。

929
00:41:06.710 --> 00:41:09.250
He's going through a security check.
他正在通过安检。

930
00:41:09.250 --> 00:41:14.550
But he also made a choice to go to the airport even if he had to miss Pam.
但他同时也做出了选择，即使可能会错过帕姆，他也要去机场。

931
00:41:14.830 --> 00:41:15.130
Yes.
是的。

932
00:41:15.230 --> 00:41:16.850
He doesn't know he's going to see Pam.
他当时并不知道自己会见到帕姆。

933
00:41:16.930 --> 00:41:17.050
Yeah.
没错。

934
00:41:17.050 --> 00:41:17.750
Which is important.
这一点很重要。

935
00:41:18.030 --> 00:41:18.550
I think so, too.
我也这么认为。

936
00:41:18.550 --> 00:41:22.070
I think it's kind of like – because he started off – everybody at this office is my family.
我觉得这有点像——因为他一开始说——办公室里的每个人都是我的家人。

937
00:41:22.070 --> 00:41:26.190
And then he gets to have this talking head where he kind of recalibrates it.
然后他有了一段采访镜头，在那里他重新调整了自己的想法。

938
00:41:26.230 --> 00:41:27.270
It's still super important.
这依然非常重要。

939
00:41:27.270 --> 00:41:29.870
But he knows who his family is going to be.
但他已经知道谁才是他真正的家人了。

940
00:41:30.590 --> 00:41:34.630
Now, you guys know that there's nothing I love more than a location report.
好了，你们都知道我最喜欢外景报道了。

941
00:41:34.630 --> 00:41:36.930
But I'm going to let Amanda S.
但我打算让阿曼达·S.

942
00:41:37.050 --> 00:41:40.070
from Rancho Santa Margarita, California, take this one.
来自加利福尼亚州兰乔圣玛格丽塔的她来介绍这一段。

943
00:41:40.430 --> 00:41:41.370
Amanda said,
阿曼达说，

944
00:41:41.530 --> 00:41:43.650
I know a bit about this location breakdown.
我对这个外景地的情况了解一些。

945
00:41:43.910 --> 00:41:48.450
The airport scene was filmed at the Ontario International Airport in Ontario, California.
机场那场戏是在加利福尼亚州安大略市的安大略国际机场拍摄的。

946
00:41:48.450 --> 00:41:53.310
I grew up in the neighboring city of Rancho Cucamonga and recognized it right away.
我在邻近的兰乔库卡蒙格市长大，一眼就认出来了。

947
00:41:53.610 --> 00:41:57.710
I don't know if they chose this airport because LAX wouldn't let you go back.
我不知道他们选这个机场是不是因为洛杉矶国际机场不让进安检区。

948
00:41:57.710 --> 00:42:04.610
But I do know that Ontario had lost a lot of traffic around this time due to the 2008 recession and ownership issues.
但我确实知道，由于2008年的经济衰退和所有权问题，安大略机场当时流失了大量客流。

949
00:42:04.610 --> 00:42:07.690
So, maybe it was just an easier option because it was so quiet.
所以，也许因为它当时很冷清，才成了一个更方便的选择。

950
00:42:07.930 --> 00:42:09.710
Well, I reached out to Randy Cordray.
好吧，我联系了兰迪·科德雷。

951
00:42:09.890 --> 00:42:11.510
He said, Amanda is right.
他说，阿曼达是对的。

952
00:42:11.830 --> 00:42:12.710
Way to go, Amanda.
干得好，阿曼达。

953
00:42:12.930 --> 00:42:13.270
Yes.
是的。

954
00:42:13.390 --> 00:42:18.290
We shot this at the Ontario airport in a closed terminal that was not open to the public.
我们在安大略机场的一个封闭航站楼拍摄，那里不对公众开放。

955
00:42:18.730 --> 00:42:20.930
Everyone you see is a hired extra.
你看到的每个人都是雇来的临时演员。

956
00:42:21.450 --> 00:42:24.670
The TSA check-in was set dressing brought in by us.
安检处是我们自己搭建的布景。

957
00:42:24.670 --> 00:42:28.310
But in order to shoot there, there were a lot of rules.
但为了在那里拍摄，有很多规定。

958
00:42:29.190 --> 00:42:33.930
Any cast or crew member who was shooting there that day got this memo, this very detailed memo,
当天在那拍摄的任何演职人员都收到了这份备忘录，一份非常详细的备忘录，

959
00:42:34.210 --> 00:42:36.390
outlining the strict rules for being there.
概述了在那里的严格规定。

960
00:42:36.610 --> 00:42:37.830
I have my memo.
我有我的那份备忘录。

961
00:42:39.450 --> 00:42:40.970
It says, hi, all.
上面写着，大家好。

962
00:42:41.130 --> 00:42:42.270
I love a memo with rules.
我喜欢有规则的备忘录。

963
00:42:42.290 --> 00:42:43.090
You know I love a memo.
你知道我喜欢备忘录。

964
00:42:43.150 --> 00:42:43.730
I love a memo.
我喜欢备忘录。

965
00:42:44.250 --> 00:42:45.010
Hi, all.
大家好。

966
00:42:45.250 --> 00:42:49.230
As we get ready to shoot at the Ontario airport, there are a few things you need to know.
在我们准备在安大略机场拍摄时，有几件事你们需要知道。

967
00:42:49.690 --> 00:42:54.370
It says, you will be working at a closed terminal but within the control of the TSA.
上面写着，你们将在一个封闭的航站楼工作，但处于美国运输安全管理局（TSA）的管控之下。

968
00:42:54.670 --> 00:42:57.470
So just because it was closed, don't think there's no rules, okay?
所以别以为因为关闭了就没规矩了，好吗？

969
00:42:58.010 --> 00:43:01.430
You had to have your government-issued ID in order to enter.
你必须持有政府签发的身份证件才能进入。

970
00:43:01.890 --> 00:43:05.010
You had to wear an office ID badge at all times.
你必须始终佩戴工作证。

971
00:43:05.650 --> 00:43:10.350
All crew members entering the airport were screened by TSA agents with dogs.
所有进入机场的工作人员都必须接受TSA特工和警犬的检查。

972
00:43:10.790 --> 00:43:11.270
What?
什么？

973
00:43:11.570 --> 00:43:11.950
Yeah.
是的。

974
00:43:12.370 --> 00:43:17.730
Wanted you to know that all explosives, firearms, and narcotics are prohibited.
想让你们知道，严禁携带任何爆炸物、枪支和毒品。

975
00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:20.510
That was bolded, all caps, and underlined.
那一行是加粗、全大写并加了下划线的。

976
00:43:20.670 --> 00:43:20.890
Okay.
好吧。

977
00:43:21.450 --> 00:43:26.670
If you have handled pyrotechnics or firearms in the last 30 days, you need to let them know
如果你在过去30天内接触过烟火或枪支，你需要告知他们，

978
00:43:26.670 --> 00:43:30.070
because that residue can live on your clothing for 30 days.
因为残留物会在你的衣服上停留30天。

979
00:43:30.970 --> 00:43:37.590
And if a dog alerts that you have any of these residues on you, you will be made to leave.
如果警犬发现你身上有这些残留物，你将被要求离开。

980
00:43:37.950 --> 00:43:38.870
Is that all?
就这些吗？

981
00:43:39.030 --> 00:43:39.630
There's more.
还有呢。

982
00:43:39.750 --> 00:43:40.570
That will happen to you?
这会发生在你身上？

983
00:43:40.770 --> 00:43:41.010
Oh.
噢。

984
00:43:41.570 --> 00:43:45.970
It doesn't sound like you'll be arrested, but you're not going to get to be in the shoot day.
听起来你不会被捕，但你没法参加当天的拍摄了。

985
00:43:46.150 --> 00:43:48.710
In the deserted terminal of Ontario Airport.
在安大略机场荒废的航站楼里。

986
00:43:49.450 --> 00:43:54.010
Once you're in the airport, bold, all caps, and underlined, do not open any doors.
一旦进入机场，加粗、全大写并加下划线：严禁打开任何门。

987
00:43:54.650 --> 00:43:57.470
If you open a door, you could be fined $11,000.
如果你打开一扇门，可能会被罚款11000美元。

988
00:43:57.990 --> 00:43:58.730
What if you have to pee?
那如果想上厕所怎么办？

989
00:43:59.070 --> 00:44:00.070
Don't open the door.
别开门。

990
00:44:00.290 --> 00:44:00.990
I don't know.
我不知道。

991
00:44:01.530 --> 00:44:02.910
You cannot open a door.
你不能开门。

992
00:44:03.050 --> 00:44:04.910
I don't think stall doors are part of that.
我觉得隔间门应该不包括在内吧。

993
00:44:04.910 --> 00:44:07.210
I meant like exterior doors.
我是说像外门那样的。

994
00:44:07.650 --> 00:44:08.690
Like a door to a bathroom.
比如通往洗手间的门。

995
00:44:09.450 --> 00:44:10.730
No, that would go into a bathroom.
不，那是通往洗手间的门。

996
00:44:10.730 --> 00:44:11.750
Can't you just pee out in the world?
你就不能在外面解决吗？

997
00:44:12.550 --> 00:44:14.390
Don't you go into an interior bathroom?
你难道不进室内的洗手间吗？

998
00:44:14.510 --> 00:44:17.150
I'm saying the door to go into the bathroom.
我是说进入洗手间的门。

999
00:44:17.210 --> 00:44:18.270
That's not included.
那不包括在内。

1000
00:44:18.690 --> 00:44:23.650
I mean, any doors, you can't just open a door and like walk around outside and have a cigarette.
我的意思是，任何门，你不能随便开一扇门然后走到外面去抽烟。

1001
00:44:23.810 --> 00:44:24.830
Go down to the tarmac.
去停机坪。

1002
00:44:24.830 --> 00:44:27.150
Once you're inside, do not open a door.
一旦进去，千万别开门。

1003
00:44:27.170 --> 00:44:29.610
Now your line makes sense to me.
现在我明白你那句台词的意思了。

1004
00:44:29.690 --> 00:44:30.790
Do you just pee out in the world?
你平时就在外面随地小便吗？

1005
00:44:30.950 --> 00:44:32.030
I was like, what is Greg saying?
我当时心想，Greg在说什么呢？

1006
00:44:32.030 --> 00:44:34.070
Doesn't everyone pee out in the world somewhere?
难道不是每个人都会在外面某个地方小便吗？

1007
00:44:35.070 --> 00:44:36.810
As opposed to just at your home?
而不是只在自己家里？

1008
00:44:38.310 --> 00:44:43.530
Bold and in italics, this memo would like you to know that the $11,000 fine is a personal
这份备忘录用加粗斜体字强调，一万一千美元的罚款是针对你个人的

1009
00:44:43.530 --> 00:44:44.290
fine to you.
罚款。

1010
00:44:44.410 --> 00:44:45.810
NBC will not be paying it.
NBC不会替你付的。

1011
00:44:45.970 --> 00:44:48.650
So if you open that door, it's on you.
所以如果你开了那扇门，后果自负。

1012
00:44:49.450 --> 00:44:56.990
And the final note is that because of the nature of work for the grip, electric, and props
最后一点，考虑到场务、灯光和道具部门的工作性质

1013
00:44:56.990 --> 00:45:00.870
department, knives will be allowed because they did have to use a knife.
允许携带刀具，因为他们确实需要用到刀。

1014
00:45:00.870 --> 00:45:04.390
However, it must be kept in your pocket when not in use.
但是，不用的时候必须放在口袋里。

1015
00:45:05.050 --> 00:45:06.810
Do not set down your knife.
不要放下你的刀。

1016
00:45:07.090 --> 00:45:08.010
Do not turn away.
不要转身离开。

1017
00:45:08.330 --> 00:45:10.470
It must go into your pocket.
必须放回口袋里。

1018
00:45:10.670 --> 00:45:13.590
If it does not go back in your pocket, that's another $11,000.
如果不放回口袋，又要罚一万一千美元。

1019
00:45:14.210 --> 00:45:14.690
Wow.
哇。

1020
00:45:15.090 --> 00:45:16.330
Thank you for your cooperation.
感谢您的配合。

1021
00:45:16.330 --> 00:45:17.790
Please call if you have any questions.
如有疑问请致电。

1022
00:45:18.050 --> 00:45:18.850
Who was that signed by?
那是谁签的名？

1023
00:45:19.030 --> 00:45:19.790
Steve Burgess.
Steve Burgess。

1024
00:45:20.650 --> 00:45:21.130
Typical.
不出所料。

1025
00:45:23.070 --> 00:45:26.870
I wonder how the airport settled on $11,000.
我在想机场是怎么定下一万一千美元这个数字的。

1026
00:45:27.410 --> 00:45:29.170
It's such a specific number.
这数字太具体了。

1027
00:45:30.410 --> 00:45:34.890
It's probably like $10,000 to one thing, and then someone gets a $1,000 cut.
可能是一万块是正经罚款，然后有人拿了一千块回扣。

1028
00:45:35.030 --> 00:45:36.230
Why is that where my brain goes?
为什么我的脑回路会是这样？

1029
00:45:36.370 --> 00:45:36.930
I don't know.
我不知道。

1030
00:45:37.130 --> 00:45:38.590
Someone's on the side hustle.
有人在搞副业。

1031
00:45:38.690 --> 00:45:39.330
Agency fee.
代理费。

1032
00:45:39.450 --> 00:45:41.970
Yeah, someone's like, add $1,000 for the reps.
是啊，肯定有人说，给代理人加一千块。

1033
00:45:43.390 --> 00:45:48.450
Well, Michael has now gone through security, and he's going to say, hey, will you guys
好吧，Michael现在已经过了安检，他会说，嘿，你们能

1034
00:45:48.450 --> 00:45:49.930
let me know if this thing ever airs?
告诉我这集什么时候播吗？

1035
00:45:50.050 --> 00:45:55.170
And then he takes off his mic pack, and he says, feels good to get this off my cheSt.
然后他摘下麦克风包，说，卸下重担的感觉真好。

1036
00:45:55.550 --> 00:45:59.310
And that's where you see him mouth the words, that's what she said.
就在那里，你看到他用口型说了那句，那是她说的。

1037
00:45:59.530 --> 00:45:59.770
Yes.
没错。

1038
00:45:59.890 --> 00:46:01.650
Greg, you got one in the episode.
Greg，你这集里用了一次。

1039
00:46:01.850 --> 00:46:03.050
Yeah, but it was a silent.
是啊，但那是无声的。

1040
00:46:03.270 --> 00:46:03.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1041
00:46:03.930 --> 00:46:04.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1042
00:46:04.190 --> 00:46:05.450
I loved it, though.
但我很喜欢。

1043
00:46:05.590 --> 00:46:08.650
You couldn't have Michael's last episode without that.
Michael的最后一集要是没有那句台词就不完整了。

1044
00:46:08.850 --> 00:46:14.610
Yeah, but it's almost like in a concert where the performer goes to their chorus and then
是啊，但这就像演唱会上表演者唱到副歌时

1045
00:46:14.610 --> 00:46:19.630
just points the mic at the crowd, and they all sing the chorus.
把麦克风指向观众，让大家一起唱副歌一样。

1046
00:46:19.810 --> 00:46:23.070
It's like everybody knew what he was going to say, so he didn't have to say it.
就像每个人都知道他要说什么，所以他根本不用说出口。

1047
00:46:23.270 --> 00:46:25.050
People just shouted at the TV.
大家对着电视就喊出来了。

1048
00:46:25.730 --> 00:46:27.150
Jenna, how was this scene for you?
Jenna，这场戏对你来说感觉如何？

1049
00:46:27.550 --> 00:46:31.490
You go running up, ask Pam, I loved that I could see your pantyhose,
你跑过去问Pam，我特别喜欢能看到你的连裤袜，

1050
00:46:31.490 --> 00:46:34.870
your commitment to wearing pantyhose all these years on the show.
你这些年来在剧中坚持穿连裤袜的敬业精神。

1051
00:46:35.230 --> 00:46:36.530
We finally made it off.
我们终于脱身了。

1052
00:46:37.070 --> 00:46:38.810
I refused to wear them.
我拒绝穿它们。

1053
00:46:38.930 --> 00:46:39.830
I never wore them.
我从没穿过它们。

1054
00:46:40.330 --> 00:46:42.350
And you have your shoes in your hand.
而且你手里还拿着鞋。

1055
00:46:42.350 --> 00:46:43.710
It's such a sweet moment.
真是个温馨的时刻。

1056
00:46:44.810 --> 00:46:45.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1057
00:46:45.670 --> 00:46:50.450
Well, a lot of people always mention how did Pam get through TSA without a ticket?
嗯，很多人总会问，帕姆是怎么没买票就通过安检的？

1058
00:46:51.150 --> 00:46:52.550
You know, how did she get through?
你知道，她是怎么过去的？

1059
00:46:52.750 --> 00:46:55.050
And I remember having that discussion on set.
我记得在片场讨论过这个问题。

1060
00:46:55.190 --> 00:46:57.470
And we did actually shoot me.
我们其实拍了我的戏份。

1061
00:46:57.470 --> 00:47:04.030
I remember there was this shot of me like running up and like pointing and like convincing them.
我记得有个镜头是我跑过去，指着那边，试图说服他们。

1062
00:47:04.430 --> 00:47:06.370
And then somehow they're like letting me through.
然后不知怎么的，他们就让我通过了。

1063
00:47:06.670 --> 00:47:08.290
And they were like, that would never happen.
但他们说，这根本不可能发生。

1064
00:47:08.570 --> 00:47:13.650
So then we just had me sort of arrive there with my shoes in my hand and everything.
所以后来我们就拍成我手里拿着鞋，带着所有东西出现在那儿。

1065
00:47:13.950 --> 00:47:18.110
There's a bunch of things that are a little like fudged there, I would say.
我觉得那里有很多地方处理得有点含糊。

1066
00:47:18.210 --> 00:47:20.470
I think Paul did a great job shooting it.
我觉得保罗拍得非常棒。

1067
00:47:20.470 --> 00:47:24.950
I think it looks very real, you know, and he had all this big time movie experience.
我觉得看起来很真实，你知道，他有那么多大制作电影的经验。

1068
00:47:25.090 --> 00:47:26.910
And he really used the extras well.
他确实很好地运用了群演。

1069
00:47:26.910 --> 00:47:29.030
And it looks like a complete functioning airport.
看起来就像一个完全运作的机场。

1070
00:47:29.910 --> 00:47:35.690
When you think about it, the security, I mean, he walked right through security into a gate, practically.
仔细想想，安检，我是说，他几乎直接穿过安检到了登机口。

1071
00:47:35.910 --> 00:47:36.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1072
00:47:36.450 --> 00:47:37.770
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

1073
00:47:37.810 --> 00:47:40.370
I don't see a lot of security that are that close.
我没见过安检离得那么近的。

1074
00:47:40.530 --> 00:47:45.270
But I mean, maybe, you know, maybe the Wilkes-Barre Airport or whatever is just like that.
但也许，你知道，也许威尔克斯-巴里机场或者别的什么地方就是那样。

1075
00:47:45.270 --> 00:47:53.710
But I would just believe there was another security thing off to the left and Pam didn't know until she got through security that he was ahead of her.
但我宁愿相信左边还有另一个安检口，帕姆在过安检前不知道他在她前面。

1076
00:47:54.090 --> 00:47:54.810
So close.
太接近了。

1077
00:47:54.970 --> 00:47:55.930
That's all I'm going to say.
我只能说这么多了。

1078
00:47:56.990 --> 00:47:58.690
She doesn't have her shoes.
她没穿鞋。

1079
00:47:58.810 --> 00:47:59.710
She's like holding her shoes.
她手里拿着鞋。

1080
00:47:59.890 --> 00:48:01.850
She's gone through security, clearly.
很明显，她已经过了安检。

1081
00:48:02.210 --> 00:48:04.390
I just chose to be okay with it.
我只是选择接受这个设定。

1082
00:48:04.530 --> 00:48:04.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1083
00:48:04.670 --> 00:48:06.790
I just needed this goodbye so desperately.
我太需要这场告别了。

1084
00:48:06.790 --> 00:48:08.050
It didn't matter to me.
对我来说这不重要。

1085
00:48:08.150 --> 00:48:08.950
And it's so beautifully framed.
而且画面构图非常美。

1086
00:48:09.070 --> 00:48:10.210
It's so visual and everything.
视觉效果各方面都很好。

1087
00:48:10.570 --> 00:48:10.850
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

1088
00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:18.930
And it's silent, which is interesting because presumably Pam would have had her microphone on, even though Michael has taken his off.
而且是静音的，这很有趣，因为按理说帕姆应该戴着麦克风，尽管迈克尔已经摘掉了。

1089
00:48:19.230 --> 00:48:19.710
In the movie theater?
在电影院里吗？

1090
00:48:20.310 --> 00:48:21.290
You think she came?
你觉得她来了吗？

1091
00:48:21.430 --> 00:48:22.390
She was in King's Speech.
她当时在看《国王的演讲》。

1092
00:48:22.510 --> 00:48:26.250
Oh, she must have clicked off her mic because she didn't want anybody to know.
哦，她一定关掉了麦克风，因为她不想让任何人知道。

1093
00:48:26.770 --> 00:48:27.730
That's a good call.
说得好。

1094
00:48:27.730 --> 00:48:28.590
I like that.
我喜欢这个解释。

1095
00:48:28.790 --> 00:48:28.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1096
00:48:28.970 --> 00:48:31.750
We often talk about, did our characters ever turn our mics off?
我们经常讨论，我们的角色有没有关过麦克风？

1097
00:48:31.850 --> 00:48:33.750
Like when we went to the bathroom, when we turned off our mic?
比如我们去洗手间的时候，有没有关掉麦克风？

1098
00:48:33.850 --> 00:48:35.050
Like we would as actors.
就像我们作为演员会做的那样。

1099
00:48:35.290 --> 00:48:35.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1100
00:48:35.610 --> 00:48:39.450
As actors, if you went to the bathroom or you went to your trailer, you'd like click your mic off.
作为演员，如果你去洗手间或者回拖车，你会关掉麦克风。

1101
00:48:39.590 --> 00:48:39.750
Yeah.
是啊。

1102
00:48:39.750 --> 00:48:43.570
Well, in answer to your question about doing this scene, I've told this story before.
嗯，关于你问我拍这场戏的事，我以前讲过这个故事。

1103
00:48:44.410 --> 00:48:45.710
This was not scripted.
这并不是剧本里写的。

1104
00:48:45.850 --> 00:48:47.770
There was nothing for us to say.
我们当时没什么台词可说。

1105
00:48:47.990 --> 00:48:52.510
And so, Paul Feig just told me to run up and tell Steve Carell goodbye.
所以保罗·费格只是让我跑过去跟史蒂夫·卡瑞尔道别。

1106
00:48:53.410 --> 00:48:54.350
Jenna to Steve.
珍娜对史蒂夫。

1107
00:48:54.630 --> 00:48:57.670
Have you ever said what you actually said or is that a mystery that you will?
你有没有说过你当时到底说了什么，还是说那将永远是个谜？

1108
00:48:57.950 --> 00:49:01.090
No, I've never really revealed exactly what I said to Steve.
没有，我从未真正透露过我当时对史蒂夫说了什么。

1109
00:49:01.310 --> 00:49:06.950
But, you know, the gist of it was just what it had meant to me to work with him over these seven years.
但你知道，大意就是这七年来与他共事对我意味着什么。

1110
00:49:06.950 --> 00:49:12.330
And I thanked him for a few personal things that he had done for me along the way.
我感谢了他一路走来为我做的一些私人的事情。

1111
00:49:12.330 --> 00:49:14.650
And we both cried and we hugged each other.
我们都哭了，还拥抱了彼此。

1112
00:49:14.890 --> 00:49:16.550
And I've said this before.
我以前也说过。

1113
00:49:16.550 --> 00:49:21.270
After that first take, we went back to Paul and he was like, okay, okay.
拍完第一条后，我们回到保罗那里，他当时说，好的，好的。

1114
00:49:21.270 --> 00:49:22.490
That was amazing.
太棒了。

1115
00:49:22.790 --> 00:49:23.650
That was so good.
太好了。

1116
00:49:24.530 --> 00:49:26.270
Could you do it a little faster?
你们能再快一点吗？

1117
00:49:26.830 --> 00:49:32.670
Because it was like four minutes of us just like sobbing every thought she'd ever had.
因为那足足有四分钟，我们俩就在那儿哭诉着她所有的心路历程。

1118
00:49:32.670 --> 00:49:34.550
Right, right, because there's no other camera.
对，没错，因为没有别的机位了。

1119
00:49:34.830 --> 00:49:34.950
It's a water.
那是水。

1120
00:49:34.950 --> 00:49:35.270
That's a water.
那是水。

1121
00:49:35.510 --> 00:49:35.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1122
00:49:36.210 --> 00:49:38.530
He's like, we're just needing to tighten it up a little.
他说，我们只需要稍微精简一下。

1123
00:49:39.190 --> 00:49:40.850
So, then it got easier.
所以，后来就容易多了。

1124
00:49:40.850 --> 00:49:42.310
We didn't do it very many times.
我们没拍多少次。

1125
00:49:42.310 --> 00:49:43.050
It got easier.
容易多了。

1126
00:49:43.310 --> 00:49:45.210
I needed the first one for me.
第一条是我自己需要的。

1127
00:49:45.310 --> 00:49:45.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1128
00:49:45.530 --> 00:49:46.550
You know, that was mine.
你知道，那是属于我的。

1129
00:49:46.990 --> 00:49:47.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1130
00:49:47.310 --> 00:49:51.730
Well, it's so often you're trying to get emotion in a take.
嗯，通常你总是试图在拍摄中投入情感。

1131
00:49:51.870 --> 00:49:56.410
And the first ones, people are working out the, you know, the dialogue or whatever.
而第一条的时候，大家还在琢磨台词什么的。

1132
00:49:56.850 --> 00:49:59.810
And then like two or three is where you really find your sweet spot.
然后第二或第三条才是你真正找到感觉的时候。

1133
00:49:59.890 --> 00:50:02.350
And then it starts to get kind of mannered and fake afterwards.
再往后就开始变得有点做作和虚假了。

1134
00:50:02.590 --> 00:50:02.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:50:02.950 --> 00:50:08.150
But it's interesting that it was like on this episode, everything was like at an 11.
但有趣的是，在这一集里，一切都像是拉满到了11分。

1136
00:50:08.530 --> 00:50:09.930
On the first take, yeah.
第一条的时候是这样，没错。

1137
00:50:10.150 --> 00:50:12.010
And then you bring it down a bit.
然后你再稍微收敛一点。

1138
00:50:12.930 --> 00:50:14.990
Well, then Pam has this talking head.
嗯，然后帕姆有这个采访镜头。

1139
00:50:15.290 --> 00:50:18.370
And I remember we did a lot of versions of this talking head.
我记得我们拍了很多个版本的采访。

1140
00:50:18.550 --> 00:50:20.170
But I love the one that we picked.
但我很喜欢我们选中的那一个。

1141
00:50:20.250 --> 00:50:21.390
It was really, really sweet.
真的很甜，很感人。

1142
00:50:21.510 --> 00:50:25.050
Although, I never felt like I nailed it.
虽然我从来没觉得我演得完美。

1143
00:50:25.050 --> 00:50:32.110
I never, I was so emotional from having shot the scene that I just couldn't, I don't know.
我从来没觉得，拍完那场戏后我情绪太激动了，以至于我无法，我不知道。

1144
00:50:32.210 --> 00:50:34.610
I just, it was hard for me, this talking head.
我只是，这个采访镜头对我来说很难。

1145
00:50:34.750 --> 00:50:35.450
Well, I disagree.
嗯，我不同意。

1146
00:50:35.450 --> 00:50:37.150
I think you totally nailed it.
我觉得你演得非常完美。

1147
00:50:37.710 --> 00:50:39.770
Connected to the plane taking off, that thing, right?
是连接到飞机起飞的那一段，对吧？

1148
00:50:39.910 --> 00:50:41.470
Or is that just, is there a cut?
还是说，中间有剪辑？

1149
00:50:41.490 --> 00:50:42.150
That's after.
那是之后的事了。

1150
00:50:42.450 --> 00:50:43.110
Oh, thank goodness.
哦，谢天谢地。

1151
00:50:43.270 --> 00:50:46.710
Can you imagine if we had to wait for the plane every time you got a take?
你能想象如果我们每次拍一条都要等飞机吗？

1152
00:50:47.330 --> 00:50:51.930
No, but we did have to wait for that plane to take off so that we could do that.
不，但我们确实得等那架飞机起飞，才能拍那个镜头。

1153
00:50:52.030 --> 00:50:53.550
And a plane never took off.
结果飞机根本没起飞。

1154
00:50:53.550 --> 00:50:58.110
We waited like an hour to get a shot of me watching a plane take off.
我们等了一个小时，就为了拍我看着飞机起飞的镜头。

1155
00:50:58.610 --> 00:51:05.530
Randy reminded me that a plane did eventually take off, but it was like a little private plane, which obviously Michael would not be on.
兰迪提醒我，后来确实有架飞机起飞了，但那是一架小型私人飞机，迈克尔显然不可能在上面。

1156
00:51:05.630 --> 00:51:06.490
So, how did we do that shot?
那么，我们是怎么拍那个镜头的？

1157
00:51:06.510 --> 00:51:07.670
We added it in poSt.
后期加进去的。

1158
00:51:08.430 --> 00:51:09.230
Fakie plane.
假飞机。

1159
00:51:09.550 --> 00:51:12.290
I just looked off at nothing.
我只是对着虚空看了一眼。

1160
00:51:13.130 --> 00:51:15.730
Another metaphor for him going up into the sky.
这也是他飞向天空的另一个隐喻。

1161
00:51:15.930 --> 00:51:16.170
See?
你看？

1162
00:51:16.390 --> 00:51:17.630
Yes, it was an important shot.
是的，那是一个很重要的镜头。

1163
00:51:17.910 --> 00:51:18.350
Yeah, I had to get that plane.
没错，我必须得拍到那架飞机。

1164
00:51:18.350 --> 00:51:21.970
He starts in the sky and ends in the sky in this episode.
他在这一集中从天空开始，又在天空结束。

1165
00:51:22.190 --> 00:51:22.350
Yeah.
是的。

1166
00:51:23.130 --> 00:51:31.530
One of the things I always love about our show is right after a big emotional moment, there's then usually this great comedic bit, sometimes dark.
我一直很喜欢我们剧的一点是，在重大的情感时刻之后，通常会紧接着一段很棒的喜剧桥段，有时还带点黑色幽默。

1167
00:51:31.730 --> 00:51:36.530
And this one is a definite foreshadowing of how D'Angelo is going to be.
而这一段绝对预示了迪安杰洛之后会是什么样。

1168
00:51:36.790 --> 00:51:38.030
There is the party.
派对开始了。

1169
00:51:38.250 --> 00:51:39.170
It's Michael's party.
这是迈克尔的欢送派对。

1170
00:51:39.310 --> 00:51:40.210
It's the next day.
已经是第二天了。

1171
00:51:40.350 --> 00:51:41.750
He hasn't shown up.
他还没出现。

1172
00:51:42.290 --> 00:51:43.830
And there's a big cake.
而且有个大蛋糕。

1173
00:51:44.070 --> 00:51:46.190
And D'Angelo's like, well, we should just have a piece, right?
迪安杰洛就说，好吧，我们应该吃一块，对吧？

1174
00:51:46.310 --> 00:51:47.530
He's, you know, might as well.
他觉得，你知道的，反正闲着也是闲着。

1175
00:51:47.730 --> 00:51:49.630
But he digs in with his hand.
但他直接用手抓着吃。

1176
00:51:49.830 --> 00:51:50.110
Yeah.
没错。

1177
00:51:50.430 --> 00:51:53.410
And he starts eating the cake and then he throws it in the trash.
他开始吃蛋糕，然后把它扔进了垃圾桶。

1178
00:51:53.450 --> 00:51:54.250
He's like, no.
他就像是说，不吃了。

1179
00:51:54.630 --> 00:51:57.230
And then he goes back in and then he does it again.
然后他又回去，又吃了一次。

1180
00:51:57.490 --> 00:51:59.530
And people are like, oh, my goodness.
大家都在想，天哪。

1181
00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:01.970
Dwight turns to Jim and goes, oh, no.
德怀特转向吉姆说，噢，不。

1182
00:52:02.530 --> 00:52:05.210
I love that moment between Dwight and Jim at the end.
我喜欢最后德怀特和吉姆之间的那个瞬间。

1183
00:52:05.510 --> 00:52:05.770
Yeah.
是的。

1184
00:52:05.830 --> 00:52:07.610
It's like the devil you know, right?
就像是“熟悉的魔鬼”，对吧？

1185
00:52:07.610 --> 00:52:10.910
You're like, why did we ever wish we would want anyone other than Michael?
你会想，我们为什么会希望迈克尔以外的人来接手？

1186
00:52:10.910 --> 00:52:13.010
Well, I guess Dwight never did, but.
嗯，我想德怀特从来没这么想过，但是。

1187
00:52:13.490 --> 00:52:16.410
But also, I love when Dwight and Jim team up.
而且我也喜欢德怀特和吉姆联手的时候。

1188
00:52:16.890 --> 00:52:20.790
And just to see like, oh, okay, it's going to be those two against this guy.
看到他们俩要联手对付这个家伙，感觉很有趣。

1189
00:52:20.910 --> 00:52:21.130
Yeah.
是的。

1190
00:52:21.390 --> 00:52:22.590
Is an interesting thing.
这很有意思。

1191
00:52:22.990 --> 00:52:27.170
When you think about it, when you watch the show now on Peacock and there are no ads and
当你现在在Peacock上观看这部剧，没有广告的时候，

1192
00:52:27.170 --> 00:52:31.330
you're just kind of watching it, that does feel like, oh, that's a weird place to end.
你只是顺着看下去，会觉得，噢，这个结尾有点奇怪。

1193
00:52:31.510 --> 00:52:35.950
But you have to remember that, you know, the show kind of ended and there was three minutes
但你必须记住，你知道，剧集原本结束时会有三分钟

1194
00:52:35.950 --> 00:52:39.550
of commercials and this is like a little bitty tag on the end.
的广告，而这只是结尾的一个小彩蛋。

1195
00:52:39.550 --> 00:52:43.330
Yeah, that's true because you used to have to write for those act breaks.
没错，确实如此，因为以前必须为那些广告间隙进行创作。

1196
00:52:43.530 --> 00:52:43.790
Yeah.
是的。

1197
00:52:44.010 --> 00:52:46.130
And now it can be viewed without them.
而现在观看时没有那些广告了。

1198
00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:47.130
Right.
对。

1199
00:52:47.190 --> 00:52:49.150
It does change the experience a little bit.
这确实稍微改变了观看体验。

1200
00:52:49.210 --> 00:52:53.210
It changes the pow a little bit because you're like, whoa, we're doing this now.
它改变了那种冲击力，因为你会想，哇，我们现在要演这个了。

1201
00:52:53.310 --> 00:52:55.290
They chose to end on the cake gag.
他们选择以蛋糕梗作为结尾。

1202
00:52:56.630 --> 00:52:57.450
That's strange.
那真奇怪。

1203
00:52:58.030 --> 00:53:03.030
One thing I wanted to share was a lot of people in the cast who didn't have scenes on particular
我想分享的一件事是，很多演员在某些日子里没有戏份，

1204
00:53:03.030 --> 00:53:07.570
days, they all would just come back, even on their day off, to watch Steve's final scenes.
但他们都会回来，即使是在休息日，也要观看史蒂夫的最后几场戏。

1205
00:53:07.870 --> 00:53:13.490
And a lot of people obviously came back for this last day, crew and producers and writers
显然，很多人都为了最后这一天赶了回来，剧组人员、制片人、编剧

1206
00:53:13.490 --> 00:53:16.970
and the cast, all there to watch these final moments.
还有演员们，大家都到场见证了这些最后的时刻。

1207
00:53:16.970 --> 00:53:20.470
And then we had a party in the warehouse to say goodbye to Steve.
然后我们在仓库举办了一场派对，向史蒂夫告别。

1208
00:53:20.670 --> 00:53:21.550
It was so perfect.
那真是太完美了。

1209
00:53:21.830 --> 00:53:24.950
Do you remember Nancy made that cake or had a cake made?
你还记得南希做了那个蛋糕，或者让人做了一个蛋糕吗？

1210
00:53:25.110 --> 00:53:25.250
Yeah.
记得。

1211
00:53:25.250 --> 00:53:29.130
And it was a giant cake in the shape of a world's best boss mug.
那是一个巨大的蛋糕，形状是“世界最佳老板”的马克杯。

1212
00:53:29.310 --> 00:53:31.490
Yeah, it was a huge coffee mug.
对，那是一个巨大的咖啡杯。

1213
00:53:31.630 --> 00:53:31.930
Yes.
没错。

1214
00:53:32.070 --> 00:53:34.370
And John had made a tribute video.
约翰还制作了一个致敬视频。

1215
00:53:34.630 --> 00:53:39.250
He had had a bunch of different people send in goodbye messages like you would have at a
他让很多人发来了告别寄语，就像你在

1216
00:53:39.250 --> 00:53:40.230
retirement party.
退休派对上会看到的那样。

1217
00:53:40.810 --> 00:53:42.830
Rain gave a speech on behalf of the caSt.
雷恩代表演员阵容发表了演讲。

1218
00:53:43.090 --> 00:53:44.450
I gave a speech, I remember.
我记得我也发表了演讲。

1219
00:53:44.610 --> 00:53:45.030
You gave a speech?
你发表了演讲？

1220
00:53:45.030 --> 00:53:46.550
If I had known you guys were talking, I would have brought it.
如果我知道你们在聊这个，我就把它带来了。

1221
00:53:46.610 --> 00:53:49.070
I think it's on my computer somewhere.
我想它应该还在我电脑里的某个地方。

1222
00:53:49.350 --> 00:53:50.870
Oh, that's so great.
哦，那太棒了。

1223
00:53:50.870 --> 00:53:55.590
Yeah, I remember there were a lot of jokes about how he could have been a dick, but he
是啊，我记得当时有很多笑话，说他本可以表现得很混蛋，但他

1224
00:53:55.590 --> 00:53:56.010
wasn't.
并没有那样做。

1225
00:53:58.030 --> 00:54:02.190
Because he had all of the, he was so important to the show.
因为他拥有所有的一切，他对这部剧来说太重要了。

1226
00:54:02.350 --> 00:54:08.570
And I think I compared him to other leads who were in the news for bad behavior or something.
我想我当时把他和其他因为行为不端而上新闻的主演做了比较，诸如此类的。

1227
00:54:08.650 --> 00:54:10.010
I can't remember the whole gist of it.
我不记得具体内容了。

1228
00:54:10.630 --> 00:54:12.030
Oh, that's so sweet.
哦，那太贴心了。

1229
00:54:12.490 --> 00:54:18.930
A big thing that happened, and this was Randy Cordray's idea, was that we retired his number
还有一件大事，这是兰迪·科德雷的主意，我们把他在通告单上的号码

1230
00:54:18.930 --> 00:54:19.910
on the call sheet.
退役了。

1231
00:54:19.910 --> 00:54:21.010
He was our number one.
他是我们的“一号”。

1232
00:54:21.190 --> 00:54:25.510
And moving forward, the call sheet started with number two forever.
从那以后，通告单永远从二号开始。

1233
00:54:25.990 --> 00:54:31.310
So it didn't matter whoever we were going to hire to ever be maybe the boss in the future.
所以无论未来我们雇佣谁来担任老板，

